{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Like stone</b> — the waters hide until they harden like stone, and the meaning is that they are not seen as waters." "<b>And the face of the deep is taken hold of</b> — the matter is a doubled question: that the waters of the deep are taken hold of, until they bind together. And some say: its meaning is that they are taken hold of upon the face of the deep, and it is close [to the meaning]."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:05.031042096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}